{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Indices and Iterators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorSequence","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/EnumeratedIterator","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SetIterator","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/StrideThroughIterator","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/StrideToIterator"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Indices-and-Iterators"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/indexingiterator"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator\/SubSequence"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases"},{"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator\/IteratorProtocol-Implementations","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator\/Sequence-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IndexingIterator"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that iterates over a collection using its indices."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IndexingIterator"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Elements"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Elements"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Collection","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Collection"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" type is the default iterator for any collection that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t declare its own. It acts as an iterator by using a collection’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indices to step over each value in the collection. Most collections in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard library use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" as their iterator."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, any custom collection type you create will inherit a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that returns an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" instance,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"making it unnecessary to declare your own. When creating a custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection type, add the minimal requirements of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol: starting and ending indices and a subscript for accessing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements. With those elements defined, the inherited "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method satisfies the requirements of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s an example of a type that declares the minimal requirements for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" structure is a fixed-size collection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that always holds two elements of a specific type."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct CollectionOfTwo<Element>: Collection {","    let elements: (Element, Element)","","    init(_ first: Element, _ second: Element) {","        self.elements = (first, second)","    }","","    var startIndex: Int { return 0 }","    var endIndex: Int   { return 2 }","","    subscript(index: Int) -> Element {","        switch index {","        case 0: return elements.0","        case 1: return elements.1","        default: fatalError(\"Index out of bounds.\")","        }","    }","    ","    func index(after i: Int) -> Int {","        precondition(i < endIndex, \"Can't advance beyond endIndex\")","        return i + 1","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t define its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Iterator"},{"type":"text","text":" associated type, it uses the default iterator type,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IndexingIterator"},{"type":"text","text":". This example shows how a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectionOfTwo"},{"type":"text","text":" instance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be created holding the values of a point, and then iterated over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let point = CollectionOfTwo(15.0, 20.0)","for element in point {","    print(element)","}","\/\/ Prints \"